From: Gesher Authors
Subject: [PATCH] Retire queued speech recognition commands on connection failure

Keep the public app-side connection queue on the main looper. An admission
failure completes each pending operation through its own callback. Late binds
release their endpoint, and a canceled wait does not start a recording.
Immediate and deferred failures follow the same ordered handler path.
Errors retain the listener selected for each command. After a session Binder
dies, its queued operations fail and the next operation can reconnect.

